## 11. Registry integrity and validation

Implement validation at both service and database levels where the actual stack supports it.

### Required integrity checks

- Unique agent IDs.
- Valid category references.
- Valid lifecycle status values.
- Valid configuration structure.
- Valid contract version.
- Valid mapping version.
- No duplicate primary mapping for a category.
- No orphaned category-agent association.
- No accidental deletion of required registry records.
- No invalid configuration updates.
- No unauthorized changes to protected identifiers.

### Initial registry validation

The initial registry must pass all of these checks:

- Exactly 29 expected agent IDs exist.
- All 29 agent IDs are unique.
- All 29 finalized category associations exist.
- Every expected category has exactly one primary agent.
- Every agent maps to its correct primary category.
- No unexpected duplicate primary mapping exists.
- All records have valid initial configuration versions and statuses.

A failed validation must produce a clear error and must not leave a partially seeded registry.

Use transactions or the database's equivalent atomic mechanism when available.

