- Track update timestamps.
- Track authorized change actors.
- Preserve enough history to identify important changes.

Where an audit system exists, integrate with it rather than creating another unrelated logging framework.

Where no audit infrastructure exists, implement only the minimum registry change-history mechanism needed for this scope.

Never record passwords, API keys, access tokens or unnecessary sensitive business data.

